// CSlopDeskFFI — the Clang module that lets Swift see `slopdesk_ffi.h`.
//
// ONE header, deliberately, even though the doors are sixteen `slopdesk_ffi_*.h` parts: the umbrella
// includes them in order, so clang assembles the same translation unit it always did, and there is
// exactly one name Swift can import. An `umbrella "."` over the directory would make every part its
// own top-level declaration and let a part that fell out of the include list keep working here while
// a `#include "slopdesk_ffi.h"` from C lost it.
//
// This module IS inside the `swift build` graph, and that is the whole point. The
// one-implementation rule says a ported module's Swift original is deleted in the same change, and
// a Rust implementation that `swift test` cannot reach would leave the Swift version alive as the
// thing actually under test — two implementations wearing one name.
//
// The cost, stated plainly: `swift build` now needs `ThirdParty/slopdesk-ffi/SlopDeskFFI.xcframework`
// to exist, so a clean checkout runs `just ffi` (or any `just build`/`test`/`check`, which depend
// on it) once before SwiftPM will resolve. cargo still never runs INSIDE `swift build`.
module CSlopDeskFFI {
    header "slopdesk_ffi.h"
    export *
}
